Hello, everyone,

Another question on the c code. The following code,
I'm trying to reformat my data from S+ ("sData") into
a 2-d data ("data") in c. The program crashes and
complains about the "bad address". I'm pretty sure the
sizes line up. Just wonder if that's to do with the
fact that I have pointer to pointers in c (float **).
Thanks very much. -- Dan

Here is the code:

-------------------------
void chgData(float * sData, long * Len, long * nVar,
float * test)
/* nVar: Num of variables including sData. */
/* Len: Length of each variable. */
/* data size is Len x nVar */
{
  long i,j,k,nn,m;
  float ** data;

  nn = *Len;
  m = *nVar;

  data = (float **) malloc((nn * m) * sizeof(float
*));

  for (i=0; i< nn; i++) { 
    for (k=0; k< m; k++) { 
       data[i][k] = sData[k*nn + i]; 
     } 
   } 

/* making sure correctness */
   test[0] = data[1][0]; 
   test[1] = data[0][2]; 
  free(data);
}


